  {
    "sha": "232fd557cfd11e1f2d265d1d638d1400ea4c31c7",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKDIzMmZkNTU3Y2ZkMTFlMWYyZDI2NWQxZDYzOGQxNDAwZWE0YzMxYzc",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-22T21:13:14Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-22T21:13:14Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(2d): resolve the adaptive pass start on the parent's API\n\nThe merge of origin/main (e313aa663, the merge of #3353) conflicts with\nthe #3355 adaptive pass start: both sides changed pocket_started and the\nAdaptive arm of pocket_over_with_relief. Main's StartSide already carries\nthe stock outline, so the branch's (start, stock) pair folds into it.\n\n- pocket.rs: pocket_started routes through pocket_started_on;\n  pocket_started_in is dropped; pocket_over_with_relief takes &StartSide,\n  adaptive_passes_from for the Adaptive arm and ring_plan otherwise.\n- pocket_hsm_start.rs: adaptive_passes_from takes the region and the\n  StartSide; each ring fallback is ring_plan, so it keeps #3316's order\n  and completeness guard. Auto stays byte for byte.\n- pocket_hsm.rs: adaptive_ordered takes the region and around_part; the\n  Auto fallback is main's plan_passes.\n- pocket_hsm_start_tests.rs: the pins call pocket_started_on with a\n  StartSide.\n- generate.rs: 2D Adaptive builds one StartSide from\n  pass_start_stock::footprint and calls pocket_started_on; the branch's\n  air_stock source is gone.\n- mod.rs, rest2d.rs: main's API and exports.\n- adaptive_pass_start.rs: the Inside pin now asserts the part-wall start\n  and that the level cuts the stock edge in air on both sides. Main's\n  ring law cuts each connected piece on its own with that piece's walls\n  last, so a level ends on the last piece's last cut, not always on the\n  edge. The other three pins are unchanged.\n- The #3355 decision file records the resolution and the pin change.\n\nRefs #3355\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>",
